- Compare against a byte-by-byte reversal approach for throughput

## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates practical bitfield packing/unpacking and rotation without branches, mirroring real-world protocol parsing.

## Key Concepts
- Field extraction with masks and shifts
- Recombination to rotate fields in place
- Boundary safety for 10-bit widths

## Code Example
```javascript
function rotateFieldsLeft32(x) {
  const A = x & 0x3FF;
  const B = (x >>> 10) & 0x3FF;
  const C = (x >>> 20) & 0x3FF;
  return (B) | (C << 10) | (A << 20);
}
```

